<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joachim Vadian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1484–1551</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Joachim von Watt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joachim Vadian, born Joachim von Watt, was a Swiss humanist scholar, physician and reformer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-gallen">St. Gallen</a>. After a career as professor and poet laureate in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, he returned home and served repeatedly as mayor of St. Gallen, leading the city's adoption of the Reformed faith in the 1520s. He also wrote histories of the city and of the Abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Saint Gall</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joachim-vadian.jpg" alt="Joachim Vadian" width="230" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joachim_Vadian.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
